[0.031, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[2;44r\u001b[2;44r\u001b[1;103s\u001b[1;1H\u001b[13S\u001b[2;44r\u001b[s\u001b[31;1H  \u001b[36m@@ -1,11 +1,17 @@\r\n\u001b[39m  \u001b[31m-# Incident 1, step 1.4 -- the fix, which is two changes and no new code.\u001b[39m\u001b[28X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# Incident 2, step 2.1 -- the readiness probe that passed review.\u001b[39m\u001b[35X\r\n   #\u001b[99X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# HEALTHZ_MODE=local: liveness answers \"is this process alive\" without leaving\u001b[39m\u001b[22X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# the process. It cannot be starved by the work the process is doing.\u001b[39m\u001b[31X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# \"Readiness should verify we can actually read our data.\" Nobody argues with\u001b[39m\u001b[23X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# that in a pull request, and at three replicas nobody notices: a scan every two\u001b[39m\u001b[20X\r\n  \u001b[32m+# seconds, three times over, is a rounding error on the database.\u001b[39m\u001b[35X\r\n   #\u001b[99X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# And the numbers get slack: 10-second period, 3-second timeout, five misses.\u001b[39m\u001b[23X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# A liveness probe should be the last resort, not the first responder -- taking\u001b[39m\u001b[21X\r\n  \u001b[31m-# a busy replica out of the load balancer is readiness' job, an"]
